## Context
Part 2 of ticket 1149 (tracker 1146), split off by the orchestrator so each PR stays under the /gaze 15-file breaker. Part 1 (1149) ships the schema, the parser's `--pr-body` mode and the `erg-pr-merge` warning.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The orchestrator and /gaze append their lines to the PR-body block as each step finishes
- [ ] /roar copies the block into the journal instead of rebuilding it from decayed evidence

## Imagine annotation (raid 2026-10-20)
Verdict PROCEED; exit criteria unchanged. Premise holds: nothing writes the block yet, so the part-1 /merge warning fires on every PR.
- Simplest path: two pure-text modes on `scripts/attribution_record.py` (`--append LINE` stdin->stdout, create-if-absent; `--extract --merged DATE` replacing `pending`). `gh` calls stay in the calling shell. Logic in the helper with tests, not SKILL.md prose (1152 showed fence edits written as prose go wrong).
- Appended block must be closed, plain three-backtick fences at column 0, so `parse_pr_body` and 1152's `fence_map` agree; an unclosed fence now refuses the merge.
- Roar's lenient `--capture` rejects `merged pending`; extract must substitute the merge date.
- Only the controller appends (seats return identity). Effort stays `not-stated` unless set at launch.
- gaze edit stays a short paragraph (tickets 1153/1154 will split gaze SKILL.md).
- Out of scope, noted: hand-run /hunt PRs get no plan/execute lines; seat identity is self-reported (1146's wider concern).

## Blind-spot findings (fold into the plan)
1. Nobody in-repo owns PR creation: define who seeds the block (create-if-absent in `--append`; raid appends only after the PR exists).
2. `erg-pr-merge` normalization PATCHes the body from a snapshot taken earlier; a gate line appended in between would be lost. Check, and re-fetch before patching if so.
3. No compare-and-swap on the body: append, read back, retry once if the line is missing.
4. Roar must read the final body via `gh pr view <N>` on the merged PR, not the commit message.

## Feasibility (raid phase 4): PASS, one WARN
- Paths verified: attribution_record.py, its two tests, raid/gaze SKILL.md, roar capture.md, design doc all exist. Planned PR: 8 files, under the 15-file breaker.
- WARN: `erg-pr-merge` line 168 snapshots BODY, and the short-ID normalization PATCH (lines 261-269) writes it back whole. It fires only when normalization changes the body, but a line appended in that window is lost. Executor: re-fetch the body immediately before that PATCH, with a test.
- Plan and first test are left to the executor's `/hunt` step; the Imagine file list is the plan of record.
